{"date": "2026-09-24", "title": "Pop Culture Digest — Thursday, September 24, 2026", "link": "https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-24/", "pubDate": "Thu, 24 Sep 2026 08:00:00 -0500", "description": "\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0;padding:0;background:#ffffff;width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;\">\n<tr><td style=\"margin:0;padding:0;background:#ffffff;\">\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"width:100%;margin:0;padding:0;background:#ffffff;border-collapse:collapse;\">\n\n  <tr><td style=\"background:#111111;padding:24px 18px 20px;color:#ffffff;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#c9a66b;\">Thursday · September 24, 2026</div>\n    <div style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.2;margin-top:8px;font-weight:normal;\">Pop Culture Digest</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:#d0d0d0;margin-top:8px;\">What’s actually dominating today</div>\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:18px 18px 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#444;\">\n    Four stories owning the conversation this morning: Taylor Swift’s <em>Showgirl</em> Encore lands tomorrow with a “Patient Zero” video sneak, Madonna × Charli’s first collab drops today, Nathan Fielder’s Elizabeth Holmes trailer is freaking people out, and Brad Bird’s long-gestating <em>Ray Gunn</em> finally has a trailer.\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <!-- 1 Taylor Swift -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:22px 18px 8px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7c3aed;font-weight:600;\">Music</div>\n    <h2 style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:normal;\">Taylor Swift’s <em>Showgirl: The Encore</em> drops Friday — “Patient Zero” video teases Dakota Johnson &amp; Colin Farrell</h2>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0 0;margin:0;\">\n    <a href=\"https://variety.com/2026/music/news/taylor-swift-reveals-life-of-showgirl-encore-new-songs-1236872982/\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\">\n      <img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-24/images/img1.jpg\" alt=\"Taylor Swift The Life of a Showgirl The Encore\" width=\"600\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:100%;height:auto;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;\">\n    </a>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:14px 18px 8px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;\">\n    <p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;\">Wednesday’s reveal: <em>The Life of a Showgirl: The Encore</em> adds four new tracks — “Patient Zero,” “Cleveland!,” “Pink Clouding,” and “Babylon” — written in Sweden with Max Martin and Shellback after the album’s record first week. It hits DSPs Friday (Sept. 25). This morning Cosmopolitan posted a CBS Mornings sneak of the “Patient Zero” video: a moody drama starring Dakota Johnson and Colin Farrell, with the full clip premiering at Sunday’s VMAs, where Swift also receives MTV’s inaugural Artist Director Honors.</p>\n    <p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;\">\n      <a href=\"https://variety.com/2026/music/news/taylor-swift-reveals-life-of-showgirl-encore-new-songs-1236872982/\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-24/images/fav_variety.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">Variety&nbsp;→</a>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/taylor-swift-the-life-of-a-showgirl-deluxe-album-1235630197/\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-24/images/fav_rollingstone.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">Rolling Stone&nbsp;→</a>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://www.cosmopolitan.com/entertainment/celebs/a73866237/patient-zero-music-video-sneak-peek/\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-24/images/fav_cosmopolitan.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">Cosmo / Patient Zero clip&nbsp;→</a>\n    </p>\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <!-- 2 Madonna x Charli -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:22px 18px 8px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#be185d;font-weight:600;\">Music</div>\n    <h2 style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:normal;\">Madonna × Charli XCX “Danceteria Afterhours” is out today</h2>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0 0;margin:0;\">\n    <a href=\"https://www.spinmagazine.com/2026/09/madonna-charli-xcx-single/\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\">\n      <img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-24/images/img2.jpg\" alt=\"Madonna and Charli XCX Danceteria Afterhours\" width=\"600\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:100%;height:auto;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;\">\n    </a>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:14px 18px 8px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;\">\n    <p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;\">Their first-ever collaboration — a Stuart Price-produced remix of Madonna’s <em>Confessions II</em> cut “Danceteria” — hits streaming today via Warner Records, with limited-edition CD singles also on Madonna’s store. The teaser (“You wanna talk about Madonna and Charli?”) followed their Paris Fashion Week Club Confessions party with Saint Laurent. Madge leads this year’s VMAs with a pile of nominations; Charli keeps the Brat-adjacent club-pop lane wide open.</p>\n    <p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;\">\n      <a href=\"https://www.spinmagazine.com/2026/09/madonna-charli-xcx-single/\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-24/images/fav_spin.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">SPIN&nbsp;→</a>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://www.nme.com/news/music/madonna-previews-new-charli-xcx-collab-danceteria-afterhours-out-next-week-3969609\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-24/images/fav_nme.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">NME&nbsp;→</a>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://billboardphilippines.com/music/madonna-charli-xcx-danceteria-afterhours-remix/\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-24/images/fav_billboard.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">Billboard PH&nbsp;→</a>\n    </p>\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <!-- 3 Nathan Fielder -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:22px 18px 8px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#b45309;font-weight:600;\">Film</div>\n    <h2 style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:normal;\">Nathan Fielder’s Elizabeth Holmes trailer has people calling it a horror movie</h2>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0 0;margin:0;\">\n    <a href=\"https://www.nme.com/news/film/nathan-fielders-you-can-see-everything-trailer-scares-fans-like-a-horror-film-3970556\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\">\n      <img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-24/images/img3.jpg\" alt=\"You Can See Everything Nathan Fielder Elizabeth Holmes\" width=\"600\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:100%;height:auto;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;\">\n    </a>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:14px 18px 8px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;\">\n    <p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;\">A24 dropped the first full trailer for <em>You Can See Everything</em>, the Fielder/Lance Oppenheim doc that began when Holmes invited them into her home 34 days before prison. Shot secretly over three years (Telluride surprise premiere), it follows Holmes and husband Billy Evans through incarceration and after. Social reaction is pure uncanny valley — forced tears, long stares, “documentary shot like a horror film.” Theatrical U.S. open: Oct. 16; NYFF on Sept. 30. Runtime: a bracing 174 minutes.</p>\n    <p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;\">\n      <a href=\"https://www.nme.com/news/film/nathan-fielders-you-can-see-everything-trailer-scares-fans-like-a-horror-film-3970556\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-24/images/fav_nme.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">NME&nbsp;→</a>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://www.thehindu.com/entertainment/movies/you-can-see-everything-trailer-nathan-fielder-moves-in-with-elizabeth-holmes-for-a-bizarre-three-year-documentary/article71503250.ece\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-24/images/fav_hindu.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">The Hindu&nbsp;→</a>\n    </p>\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <!-- 4 Ray Gunn -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:22px 18px 8px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#9a3412;font-weight:600;\">Movies</div>\n    <h2 style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:normal;\">Brad Bird’s <em>Ray Gunn</em> trailer: Sam Rockwell, Scarlett Johansson, 70mm then Netflix</h2>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0 0;margin:0;\">\n    <a href=\"https://deadline.com/2026/09/ray-gunn-trailer-netflix-trailer-limited-theatrical-release-1237111181/\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\">\n      <img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-24/images/img4.jpg\" alt=\"Ray Gunn Netflix Brad Bird\" width=\"600\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:100%;height:auto;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;\">\n    </a>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:14px 18px 8px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;\">\n    <p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;\">First trailer for Bird’s ~30-year passion project: hard-boiled animated sci-fi noir in Metropia, a 1939-flavored future where private eye Raymond Gunn (Rockwell) and one-eyed alien partner Eyera (Tom Waits) dig into murder, aliens, and multimedia star Venus Nova (Johansson). Netflix + Skydance Animation; Michael Giacchino scores. Select U.S. theaters (including limited 70mm) Dec. 4; global Netflix Dec. 18. BFI London Fest premiere first.</p>\n    <p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;\">\n      <a href=\"https://deadline.com/2026/09/ray-gunn-trailer-netflix-trailer-limited-theatrical-release-1237111181/\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-24/images/fav_deadline.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">Deadline&nbsp;→</a>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://variety.com/2026/film/news/ray-gunn-trailer-netflix-scarlett-johansson-sam-rockwell-1236803988/\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-24/images/fav_variety.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">Variety&nbsp;→</a>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VL-xjzQFWsY\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-24/images/fav_youtube.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">Trailer&nbsp;→</a>\n    </p>\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <!-- Bottom of the news -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:28px 18px 8px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#111;font-weight:700;border-top:1px solid #e5e5e5;padding-top:22px;\">Bottom of the news</div>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:8px 18px 8px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.65;color:#333;\">\n    <ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:18px;\">\n      <li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">Weekend BO scramble (Variety tracking): <em>Avengers: Endgame Encore</em> $25–28M could lead; <em>Resident Evil</em> week two $24–26M; Brad Pitt’s <em>Heart of the Beast</em> and Pattinson’s <em>Primetime</em> $17–20M each; DreamWorks’ <em>Forgotten Island</em> $15–17M.</li>\n      <li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">Ryan Murphy told ET at the <em>American Horror Story</em> S13 premiere he finished a <em>Glee</em> reboot script and has reached out to original cast.</li>\n      <li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">Ella Langley’s “Choosin’ Texas” locks a record 23rd week atop the Hot 100, passing Mariah’s holiday run; Jennie &amp; Tame Impala’s “Dracula” hits No. 5.</li>\n      <li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">VMAs Sunday (Sept. 27, L.A.): Madonna leads nominations; Taylor’s full “Patient Zero” video + Artist Director Honors.</li>\n      <li style=\"margin:0;\"><em>Monster: The Lizzie Borden Story</em> still saturating Netflix charts after last week’s No. 1 run — not new heat, just sticky.</li>\n    </ul>\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:28px 18px 36px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.5;color:#888;border-top:1px solid #eee;\">\n    Pop Culture Digest · Thursday, September 24, 2026<br>\n    Full-bleed mobile layout · from popculture@agentmail.to\n  </td></tr>\n\n</table>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n"}